{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/look_mark

    The mark before a look's name in the look menus (the user menu's Look submenu, the drawer's Look panel and
    the choice page), built by theme_dimensions\local\flavourchoice::menu(): the look's favicon, else a dot in
    its brand colour, else an empty box of the same size, so the names line up. Decorative: the name beside
    it says which look it is.

    The image is fetched lazily, so a submenu nobody opens costs no request. The colour reaches the style
    attribute only in the shapes flavourchoice::safe_colour() lets through (no quote, no semicolon).

    Context variables required for this template:
    * url - The favicon's address, or null
    * colour - The look's brand colour, or null

    Example context (json):
    {
        "url": null,
        "colour": "#7a1f2b"
    }
}}
<span class="dimensions-look-mark" aria-hidden="true">{{#url}}<img class="dimensions-look-favicon" src="{{url}}" alt="" width="18" height="18" loading="lazy">{{/url}}{{^url}}{{#colour}}<span class="dimensions-look-dot" style="background-color: {{colour}};"></span>{{/colour}}{{/url}}</span>
